    "long_instructions": "Before you build anything, it helps to sketch out your plan first, the same way a programmer storyboards before writing code.\r\n\r\nDo This:\r\n- Pick a topic you care about. \r\n- Drag five label boxes from the tray into your design area, three `string`, one `int`, one `bool`.\r\n- Sketch a small card or scene around them that shows off your topic.\r\n- Type your own label into each box (for example: a name, a color, or a mascot for the strings) and draw an arrow from each one to the part of your sketch it describes.\r\n- Save your sketch to your Backpack when you're finished. You'll import it in the next lesson.",
